Package: statskey-fleetd
Version: 0.1.0-2
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: StatsKey Engineering <engineering@statskey.com>
Homepage: https://statskey.com
Depends: systemd (>= 255), apparmor, git | git-core, adduser, ca-certificates
Description: privileged Fleet execution service for StatsKey workers
 statskey-fleetd is the privileged Linux Fleet execution service. It is the
 only component permitted to execute Fleet jobs on Ubuntu machines: a small
 root daemon that owns helper attestation, coordinator-signed execution
 tickets, lease timers, and every job cgroup, plus an unprivileged agent
 that polls the coordinator and requests job starts over a root-owned
 control socket.
 .
 All repository-controlled code runs as a per-job DynamicUser inside a
 non-delegated cgroup with an enforcing AppArmor profile; even a
 compromised controller or coordinator can authorize only an unprivileged
 sandbox, never root execution.
 .
 Services stay dormant after installation: the package enables but does not
 start any unit, and nothing executes until the device is paired
 (statskey-fleet-enroll) and helper attestation succeeds against
 coordinator policy.
